    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $2,875 (Amazon, 6 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":2875,"high":2875},
    specs: "30% incline and decline training · 22 in. wide belt · 10 in. touchscreen console · cushioned deck (listing)",
    pros: [
      "A 30% incline with decline training, the T5 Ultra’s two headline features",
      "A 22-inch-wide belt on an extra-long cushioned deck, per the listing",
      "A 10-inch colour touchscreen with map-based programming",
    ],
    cons: [
      "An older model: the listing refers to iFit Live, an earlier name for iFIT",
      "The listing gives no top speed, weight rating or warranty; ask the seller",
      "About $1,000 more than the T5 Ultra at Yesoul",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The closest Amazon match for incline plus decline, but an older design whose warranty and condition you must confirm first.",
    description: "The T5 Ultra is sold through Yesoul's own store rather than on Amazon. The closest machine we found on Amazon for its pairing of a 30% incline with decline is FreeMotion's i11.9, an earlier incline trainer still listed with a price. The listing is short: it describes an extra-long, cushioned deck, a 10-inch colour touchscreen, 30% incline and decline training, a 22-inch-wide running belt, and interactive iFit Live and Google Maps programming. iFit Live was the earlier name of what is now iFIT, which tells you the design dates from several years ago, and the T5 Ultra's built-in fan and heart-rate Zone 2 features have no equivalent here. The listing gives no top speed, no maximum user weight, no motor rating and no warranty, and we could not confirm those for this listing from a second source, so none is on the card. Before buying, ask the seller whether the machine is new, who honours the warranty and for how long, and whether the console's connected features still work. Amazon listed it at $2,875 on 6 November 2026, as checked for our incline trainer guide.",
  },
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Brands", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/brands/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Yesoul Treadmills", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/yesoul-treadmills/" },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is Yesoul a good treadmill brand?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Yesoul is a credible brand with published figures and terms, but its treadmills have little independent long-term coverage. The T3S Plus is a compact walking and jogging machine with a big screen and a one-year warranty; the T5 series, on sale since June 2026, is a full-size treadmill with a 30% incline and a five-year frame warranty.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How much is the Yesoul T3S Plus treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Yesoul listed the T3S Plus at $799.99, against a stated $1,199.99, on 5 November 2026. Best Buy had shown it at $699.99 in search results. Prices change often, so compare the delivered price and return terms where you buy.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Does the Yesoul T3S Plus need a subscription?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "No. Yesoul says wired screen mirroring from your phone is free, unlimited and needs no paid Yesoul membership; the app account you register is free. Your phone must support video output over the cable, and Yesoul lists some recent iPhones as unsupported.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What is the difference between the Yesoul T5 Plus, Max and Ultra?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "All three share a 20 by 60-inch deck, a 4.5 HP peak, 2.0 HP continuous motor, 12.4 mph and a 30% incline. The Plus mirrors your phone; the Max adds a touchscreen with native apps and an AI camera; the Ultra adds a -3% decline and a built-in fan.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What warranty do Yesoul treadmills have?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "The T3S Plus has a 12-month limited warranty. The T5 series has five years on the frame, three on the motor and 12 months on parts and labour, according to Yesoul’s specification page.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Can I return a Yesoul treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "From Yesoul’s own store, the T3S Plus has a 14-day home trial, with return shipping and a $100 restocking fee for a non-quality return. The T5 has a 30-day home trial with a $300 return shipping fee. Purchases from other retailers follow that retailer’s policy.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      author: { "@type": "Person", "@id": "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#shaheer-ali-khan", name: "Shaheer Ali Khan", honorificSuffix: "PhD", jobTitle: "Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist", url: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#who", sameAs: ["https://www.linkedin.com/in/shaheer-ali-khan-data/"], worksFor: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" } },
      datePublished: "2026-11-05",
      dateModified: "2026-11-05",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" },
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      ...(product.brand ? { brand: { "@type": "Brand", name: product.brand } } : {}),
      ...(product.image ? { image: product.image.url } : {}),
      ...(product.priceBounds
        ? {
            offers: {
              "@type": "AggregateOffer",
              priceCurrency: "USD",
              lowPrice: product.priceBounds.low,
              highPrice: product.priceBounds.high,
              url: product.amazonUrl,
            },
          }
        : {}),
    })),
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: 4,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: `https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/yesoul-treadmills/#${product.id}`,
      })),
    },
  ],
};

// "More in" links: the other pages in this article's hub group.
const HERE = "/yesoul-treadmills/";
const HUB = SECTIONS.find((s) => s.slug === "brands");
const GROUP = HUB?.groups.find((g) => g.pages.some((p) => p.url === HERE)) ?? HUB?.groups[0];
const MORE = (GROUP?.pages ?? []).filter((p) => p.url !== HERE).slice(0, 6);
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} | Treadmill Reviews USA`}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: "2026-11-05",
    modifiedTime: "2026-11-05",
    author: "Shaheer Ali Khan",
    section: "Fitness Equipment",
    tags: [
      "yesoul treadmill",
      "yesoul treadmill review",
      "yesoul treadmill reviews",
      "yesoul t3s plus treadmill",
      "yesoul treadmills",
      "yesoul t5 max",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "Best Value Screen: Yesoul T3S Plus", link: PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl }}
>
  <article class="ed-article" data-template="editorial">
    <div class="ed-col">
      <nav class="ed-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/brands/">Brands</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        <span>Brand Guide</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="ed-title">Yesoul Treadmills: A Buyer’s Guide to the T3S Plus and T5</h1>
      <p class="ed-dek">
        Yesoul made its name with screen-equipped exercise bikes and now sells two quite different treadmill lines in the US: the folding T3S Plus with a 21.5-inch screen, and the new T5 series with a 60-inch deck and a 30% incline. This guide sets out what each costs on the day, which figures we could confirm, and what the trial, return and warranty terms actually say.
      </p>

      <!-- Byline -->
      <div class="ed-byline">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="44" height="44" />
        <div class="ed-byline-text">
          By <a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a><br />
          Updated November 5, 2026 · Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS
        </div>
        <a href="#top-picks" class="btn-ghost">View products</a>
      </div>
      <p class="ed-disclosure">
        We research every product on this page independently. If you buy through our links, we may earn a
        commission at no cost to you. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Learn more about how we review.</a>
      </p>

      <figure class="ed-hero">
        <div class="ed-hero-collage">
          <a href="#yesoul-t3s-plus"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/413KgWQ9RnL._SL500_.jpg" alt="Yesoul T3S Plus" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#therun-20-auto-incline"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41YnGG85+YL._SL500_.jpg" alt="THERUN 20% Auto Incline Treadmill" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#sunny-versatile-treadmill"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41DuYz0yB9L._SL500_.jpg" alt="Sunny Health &amp; Fitness Versatile Treadmill" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
        </div>
        <figcaption>Yesoul T3S Plus · THERUN 20% Auto Incline Treadmill · Sunny Health &amp; Fitness Versatile Treadmill</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="ed-body prose prose-lg">
        <p class="ed-lead">
          Most people searching for a "Yesoul treadmill review" have seen one of two machines: a folding
          treadmill with a big screen on top, at a price far below a Peloton or NordicTrack with a similar
          screen, or a new treadmill advertising a 30% incline and heart-rate-controlled Zone 2 training. Both
          are Yesoul’s, they are aimed at different buyers, and they come with quite different return and
          warranty terms. Independent hands-on reviews of either are still scarce, so this guide concentrates on
          what can be checked: the published figures, where they agree, and the terms you would be buying under.
        </p>

        <section id="top-picks" class="ed-toppicks not-prose">
          <h2>Our top picks:</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best Value Screen:</span> <a href="#yesoul-t3s-plus">Yesoul T3S Plus</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Closest on Amazon:</span> <a href="#therun-20-auto-incline">THERUN 20% Auto Incline Treadmill</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[1].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Closest on Amazon:</span> <a href="#sunny-versatile-treadmill">Sunny Health & Fitness Versatile Treadmill</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[2].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Closest on Amazon:</span> <a href="#freemotion-i11-9">FreeMotion i11.9 Incline Trainer</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[3].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <aside class="ed-note not-prose">
          <span class="ed-note-k">What we checked</span>
          <strong class="text-gray-900">What we checked, and what we have not done.</strong> On
          5 November 2026 we read every treadmill and walking-pad listing in Yesoul’s US store
          (yesoulfitness.com), including the price each showed that day and whether it could be ordered, the
          specification tables on the T3S Plus, T5 Plus, T5 Max and T5 Ultra pages and the T5 Max specification
          page, and Yesoul’s refund, shipping and warranty text. We compared those with independent sources:
          Best Buy’s listings for the T3S Plus, a 31 October 2026 comparison published by Sole (a competing
          treadmill maker, so not neutral), Consumer Reports’ listing of the T3S Plus in its treadmill ratings
          (behind a paywall we did not pass), and the US Consumer Product Safety Commission’s recall database.
          Best Buy’s and Amazon’s product pages would not load for us that day, so their prices are quoted only
          where search results showed them. Figures on the T3S Plus card are those on which Yesoul and at least
          one independent source agree; the rest are attributed to Yesoul in the text. The three alternative
          cards carry the figures of their Amazon listings as checked on 6 November 2026 for our incline
          trainer and auto-incline treadmill guides. We have not tested a
          Yesoul treadmill. Prices change often, so confirm them before you order. As an Amazon Associate we earn
          from qualifying purchases.
        </aside>

        <nav class="ed-toc not-prose" aria-label="In this guide">
          <h2>In this guide</h2>
          <ol>
            <li><a href="#short-answer">Is a Yesoul Treadmill Worth Buying? The Short Answer</a></li>
            <li><a href="#who-yesoul-is">Who Yesoul Is, and Where It Sells</a></li>
            <li><a href="#current-range">The Yesoul Treadmill Range on 5 November 2026</a></li>
            <li><a href="#t3s-plus">Yesoul T3S Plus Review: What the Figures Say</a></li>
            <li><a href="#t5-series">The Yesoul T5 Series: Plus, Max and Ultra</a></li>
            <li><a href="#warranty-returns">Yesoul Warranty, Home Trial and Returns</a></li>
            <li><a href="#membership">Do You Need a Yesoul Membership?</a></li>
            <li><a href="#safety">Recalls and Safety</a></li>
            <li><a href="#who-should-buy">Who Should Buy a Yesoul Treadmill, and the Alternatives</a></li>
            <li><a href="#faq">Frequently asked questions</a></li>
          </ol>
        </nav>

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Is a Yesoul Treadmill Worth Buying? The Short Answer</h2>
<p>
            <strong>A Yesoul treadmill is worth considering if what you want is a large screen at a modest price
            (the T3S Plus) or a full-size deck with an unusually steep incline (the T5 series), and you are
            comfortable buying a machine with little independent long-term coverage.</strong> The T3S Plus is a
            walking and jogging machine with a short belt and a one-year warranty. The T5 series is a different
            class of treadmill, with a 60-inch deck, a published continuous motor rating and a five-year frame
            warranty.
          </p>
          <p>
            Yesoul’s appeal is that it does not lock its screens behind a subscription. The T3S Plus mirrors your
            phone for free, and the T5 Max and Ultra run their own apps. That is a real difference from
            NordicTrack, ProForm and Peloton, whose screens are built around a paid membership, and it is why
            Yesoul turns up in searches for <a href="/best-peloton-alternatives/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Peloton alternatives</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            The caution is evidence. When we checked on 5 November 2026 we could find no full independent
            hands-on review of the T3S Plus or any T5 model from a major outlet; Consumer Reports lists the T3S
            Plus in its ratings, but behind a paywall. The T5 series only went on sale in the US in June 2026. That
            does not make the machines bad, but it means you are relying on Yesoul’s published figures and its
            trial period more than you would with an established treadmill brand. Buy where you can return it
            easily, and use the trial.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you only want the recommendation: the <a href="#yesoul-t3s-plus" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">T3S Plus</a> for walking and jogging with a big screen, the <a href="#t5-series" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">T5 Plus</a> for steep incline walking and running on a full deck, and the <a href="#t5-series" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">T5 Max</a> only if you want the screen
            to run apps itself.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="who-yesoul-is" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Who Yesoul Is, and Where It Sells</h2>
<p>
            Yesoul is best known for its exercise bikes, the G1M Plus and G1M Max among them, which pair a
            budget-to-mid-price frame with a large screen. Its US store also sells a rower, a <a href="/best-recumbent-bikes/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>recumbent bike</a>,
            treadmills and walking pads, accessories and multi-machine bundles. Yesoul’s US website does not say
            where the company is based or who owns it, and its footer gives only "Yesoul Fitness". Support runs
            through a help centre, a ticket form and email.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Where Yesoul treadmills are sold.</strong> Yesoul sells direct through its own US store,
            which offers free standard shipping on eligible orders. The T3S Plus also appears <a href="/best-buy-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>at Best Buy</a> and on
            Walmart’s marketplace. Amazon would not load for us on 5 November 2026, so we could not confirm which
            Yesoul treadmills it carries; the Amazon buttons on this page search for each model by name. Yesoul’s store also carries
            distributor listings marked "not for customer", including one for the T3S Plus at $1,199, which is the
            price retail partners are pointed to rather than a price you would pay.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Why the seller matters.</strong> Yesoul’s return policy, the 14 and 30-day home trials and
            the price-drop refund on the T5 apply to orders from Yesoul’s own store. A T3S Plus from Best Buy, or
            a Yesoul bought from any other retailer, follows that retailer’s return terms instead, which can be better or worse.
            Read our guide to <a href="/treadmill-return-policies/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmill return policies</a> before deciding where to buy, and our guide to <a href="/buying-a-treadmill-on-amazon/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">buying a treadmill on Amazon</a> if a marketplace seller is involved.
          </p>
